1
00:00:01,320 --> 00:00:03,660
Really, this is starting to annoy me.

2
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:08,257
Why do you insist on struggling when
there is nothing to gain from it?

3
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:11,105
It should be obvious by
now that you have lost.

4
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:14,477
Why do you choose to resist
when the outcome is clear?

5
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,266
Your actions are meaningless.

6
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:21,360
Whether we choose to die on our
knees or with a sword in our hand,

7
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:23,187
it's our actions that count.

8
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:25,422
That's what being human's about.

9
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:37,780
You prefer black like a knight
from the dark territory?

10
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:41,817
Well boy if you wish to
continue suffering so

11
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:44,557
then i shall make yours
very long and cruel!

12
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:47,517
Beyond anything you can
imagine you'll be in

13
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:50,457
such misery you'll be
begging me for death!

14
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:56,680
That won't be enough to
make up for my stupidity.

15
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:03,677
It's a dream of a blue light.

16
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:05,337
Let's go back

17
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:12,200
to the moon.

18
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,417
Your voice has no place in place.

19
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:19,377
No one has taught me.

20
00:01:19,460 --> 00:01:22,140
It's a rule.

21
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:26,340
When i was young i was strong.

22
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,332
I'm going to be a dream.

23
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:33,580
I'm going to find the
way I'm looking for you.

24
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:38,917
I'm going to cry.

25
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,117
I'm going to break the edge of the world.

26
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:45,597
I'm going to be a strong,

27
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:48,900
strong, strong, strong, strong.

28
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:12,737
I'll see you

29
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:17,140
next time.

30
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:34,940
The High Norkia style.

31
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:39,225
She's going to try and
kill me with one strike.

32
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:04,400
Yes, a one-handed forehead sword skill.

33
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:07,057
It's called vertical square, is it not?

34
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:08,600
Sword skill?

35
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:10,540
How'd she know that term?

36
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:13,620
Maybe she got it from Eugeo's memories.

37
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:17,440
Alright, I'll use something
I never showed him.

38
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:19,880
A combo with more than four hits!

39
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:38,820
Mine was a six-hit skill
called Crucifixion.

40
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:41,990
No way.

41
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:58,480
A one-hit skill, Sugou.

42
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:04,697
There is nothing I do
not know about the system

43
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:07,251
which drives the properties of this world.

44
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:08,470
Damn it.

45
00:04:08,553 --> 00:04:10,040
That's not like you.

46
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:12,800
You chill.

47
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:15,470
Kirito.

48
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:29,097
Integrity Knights aren't the only
ones who lost their memories.

49
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:30,240
We did, too.

50
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,380
Something very important.

51
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:37,880
You, Alice, and I were born in Wulid
and grew up together. Remember?

52
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:41,380
Yeah, I remember it now.

53
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:45,387
I was right there with you in
the square when Alice was taken.

54
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,180
I couldn't move.

55
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:49,000
I felt so helpless.

56
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:50,940
But not you.

57
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:52,540
You were so brave.

58
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:55,269
You charged in and
stood up to that knight.

59
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,190
Mewtwo.

60
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:06,507
This time, I'm going to help you
like I should have back then.

61
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:11,380
This time, we'll save Alice. Come on.

62
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:16,990
Kirito.

63
00:05:17,073 --> 00:05:17,903
On your feet.

64
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,177
You can do it.

65
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:23,720
Stand up as many times as it takes.

66
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:43,640
You can do it.

67
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:47,457
Get up, my best friend.

68
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:51,860
And my hero.

69
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:03,720
Yeah, for you, I'll stand
as many times as it takes.

70
00:06:15,340 --> 00:06:17,420
Honestly, you have lost.

71
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,405
Why do you continue to resist?

72
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:23,837
Because I can.

73
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:25,700
It's why I'm still here.

74
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:27,980
And I won't stop till you're gone.

75
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:30,960
This world belongs to me.

76
00:06:31,340 --> 00:06:34,600
How dare you come here
uninvited and defy my rule?

77
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:36,880
On your knees!

78
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:38,660
Offer your head to me!

79
00:06:39,060 --> 00:06:40,178
Accept your defeat!

80
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:48,337
No way.

81
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:50,900
You're not a ruler. You're a thief.

82
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:54,640
You don't love this world or
the people who live in it.

83
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:57,360
So you have no right to be in charge!

84
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:07,560
To love is to rule, and I love
everything, and rule everything.

85
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:41,660
How dare you?

86
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:48,040
How dare you?

87
00:07:59,820 --> 00:08:01,220
Ah!

88
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:20,437
CURSE YOU!!!

89
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:21,640
CURSE YOU!!!

90
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,460
Not yet.

91
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:37,220
Not yet!

92
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:09,080
In the end, neither sword was metal.

93
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:13,160
How foolish.

94
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:15,680
I did not expect this outcome.

95
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:25,740
Even if I gathered up every spatial resource
here, my wound is too great to heal.

96
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:31,380
Well, at this point, I have no choice.

97
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,260
Wait, where are you?

98
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:47,040
It is much earlier than I had planned.

99
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:50,955
Nevertheless, it is time for me to go.

100
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:04,060
Farewell, little boy.

101
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:10,740
For now, the next time we
meet, shall be in your world.

102
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:12,680
What? No!

103
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:19,740
Your remnants!

104
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:22,180
Don't leave me here!

105
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:24,100
Take me with you!

106
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:26,570
Ah!

107
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:32,918
I'm go, you cretin!

108
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:35,160
Let me go this instant!

109
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:40,320
At last, I can become one
with you, your Revenant!

110
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:41,810
You...

111
00:10:41,893 --> 00:10:45,480
disgusting clown! No!

112
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:47,050
No!

113
00:10:47,133 --> 00:10:47,963
My administrator!

114
00:10:49,860 --> 00:10:51,980
My lady!

115
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:15,240
I did love it.

116
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:18,460
I loved all of it.

117
00:11:31,260 --> 00:11:34,000
Oh, it's over.

118
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:41,160
Yu-Gi-Oh.

119
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:52,560
Please work.

120
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:54,357
Stop bleeding.

121
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:56,820
Heal, goddammit! Come on!

122
00:11:57,380 --> 00:12:00,020
You can't die! Yu-Gi-Oh!

123
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:10,220
Stay cool, Kirito.

124
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:12,220
Yu-Gi-Oh, let go.

125
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:14,362
Come on, I'm trying to heal you.

126
00:12:15,260 --> 00:12:16,400
Don't bother.

127
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:17,860
It's fine.

128
00:12:18,460 --> 00:12:19,290
Really.

129
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:20,600
Leave it.

130
00:12:20,760 --> 00:12:21,877
What are you saying?

131
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:23,489
I'm not gonna let you die!

132
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:28,700
No, this is for the best it has to be.

133
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:34,040
Otherwise, you and I, we
would have fought over Alice.

134
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:39,820
Me, to get back the memory
of the Alice I knew.

135
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:45,980
And you, to save Alice the Night's soul.

136
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:49,080
Then get up and fight!

137
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:52,066
I'm gonna heal you and
then, then we'll fight!

138
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:55,080
You're way stronger than me. Do it.

139
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:57,560
Do it for the old Alice's sake.

140
00:12:58,220 --> 00:12:59,050
Fight me.

141
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:03,660
I can't fight with a broken sword.

142
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:09,500
Besides, I was weak and
gave in to Administrator.

143
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,900
I tried to kill you.

144
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:17,180
This is how I can pay for that sin.

145
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:18,380
Like I care.

146
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:20,197
You weren't in your right mind anyway.

147
00:13:20,280 --> 00:13:24,500
You fought back and snapped yourself
out of it like the badass you are.

148
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:28,157
If it wasn't for you, we
couldn't have been Administrator.

149
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,557
So you got nothing to feel guilty about.

150
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:32,228
You got nothing to pay for.

151
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:36,560
I wish that were true.

152
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:42,740
I always wished I could be more like you.

153
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:49,000
You're so brave and everyone loves you.

154
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:53,040
I-I-Alice does, too.

155
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:55,660
Now I know.

156
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:59,560
Love isn't something you get.

157
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:02,800
It's something you give.

158
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:05,480
Alice taught me that.

159
00:14:10,580 --> 00:14:12,400
I don't see you working.

160
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:16,060
Look, I'm almost done
making my part of it.

161
00:14:16,380 --> 00:14:17,700
How far did you get?

162
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:19,960
I'm way further along than you.

163
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:22,537
The guard's all that's left.

164
00:14:22,620 --> 00:14:26,020
Then let's stay here and keep
working until we finish it!

165
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:29,680
But like, what if he comes looking?

166
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:30,797
Let's go back.

167
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:32,157
But we're almost finished.

168
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:35,597
Let's stay, just a bit longer, please.

169
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:37,277
Hmm, okay.

170
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:40,380
You win, but we should still hurry it up!

171
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:46,560
All done! So am I

172
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:50,140
Wait, you've been here this whole time?

173
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,620
What you two doing?

174
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:55,360
Um, nothing.

175
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,620
It's three days too early, but oh well.

176
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:05,980
Happy birthday, Eugeo!

177
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:10,530
Is...

178
00:15:10,613 --> 00:15:11,800
is that for me?

179
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:16,438
It's no match for the real thing,
like the one your big brother's got.

180
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:22,365
Still, this one's better than any of the
wooden swords the shop and town carries.

181
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:33,160
It's wonderful.

182
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:35,700
It's beautiful.

183
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:37,800
I'll take good care of it.

184
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:39,420
Thank you both.

185
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:43,300
I never got a birthday gift
that made me so, so happy.

186
00:15:44,020 --> 00:15:45,600
What are you crying for?

187
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:47,680
I wasn't!

188
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,150
See?

189
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:01,350
Wait!

190
00:16:02,760 --> 00:16:06,113
Us three grew up together,
and we're the best of friends.

191
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:10,860
We're going different ways now,
but our memories will live forever.

192
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:13,420
We'll be with you, forever.

193
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,430
You see?

194
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:16,840
It's fine.

195
00:16:20,420 --> 00:16:21,250
You see?

196
00:16:21,333 --> 00:16:22,200
It's fine.

197
00:16:23,220 --> 00:16:25,320
So don't cry, Kirito.

198
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:28,520
Well, like you said, you're not gone.

199
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:30,740
You'll be here forever.

200
00:16:31,340 --> 00:16:32,760
Forever and ever.

201
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:36,380
The best of... ...friends.

202
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,860
Kirito, you there?

203
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:42,480
Where'd you go?

204
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:47,040
I'm here. I'm right here.

205
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:51,040
Oh, I see now.

206
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:54,580
Stars sparkling in the dark.

207
00:16:56,180 --> 00:17:01,900
The night sky above the Giga
Cedar was full of stars.

208
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:06,720
Your sword sparkles like that.

209
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:11,297
Hey, how's that for a name?

210
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:14,600
Call it the Night Sky Blade.

211
00:17:16,080 --> 00:17:17,492
Yeah, that's a good one.

212
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:19,660
Thank you, Ujiyo.

213
00:17:20,320 --> 00:17:22,120
You're like the night sky,

214
00:17:23,620 --> 00:17:28,960
wrapping this sorry world in your stars.

215
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:50,840
I guess this is for the best, huh? It is.

216
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:53,394
We can leave the rest to those two now.

217
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:57,054
I'm sure they'll guide the
world in the right direction.

218
00:17:57,840 --> 00:17:58,670
Okay.

219
00:17:58,753 --> 00:18:00,100
Well then, you ready?

220
00:18:00,740 --> 00:18:01,570
Yes.

221
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:17,760
Thank you.

222
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:04,680
Kick-Walka!

223
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:06,700
Kick-Walka! Kick-Up!

224
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:12,490
TIGUOKA!!!

225
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:19,117
Lieutenant Colonel, the
door's been breached.

226
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:20,200
We have to leave.

227
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:22,477
They'll be in the control room any second.

228
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:24,089
I'm shutting the bulkhead.

229
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:25,250
No, wait!

230
00:19:25,333 --> 00:19:26,697
Just give me a couple minutes.

231
00:19:26,780 --> 00:19:28,956
I have to sort a few things out here.

232
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:32,040
What the...?

233
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:34,497
Higa, how long till we're locked down?

234
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:36,317
I need another 80...

235
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:38,220
No, 70 seconds! What?

236
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:39,660
Holy crap!

237
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:42,900
Hey, Keeks, it's a call
from the Underworld.

238
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:44,990
It's...

239
00:19:45,073 --> 00:19:46,520
Dude, it's him!

240
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:49,240
It's Kirigaya! What? Really?

241
00:19:50,220 --> 00:19:51,380
Kirito! Stop!

242
00:20:02,260 --> 00:20:04,380
Come in, Kirito! Are you there?

243
00:20:04,580 --> 00:20:06,140
Yeah, I'm here.

244
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:07,797
You know what you've done?

245
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:08,710
Huh?

246
00:20:08,793 --> 00:20:09,760
You son of a bitch!

247
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:12,297
Can we please save the insults for later?

248
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:14,980
Right now, I need you
to listen to me. What?

249
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:17,480
I hear shooting.

250
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:18,661
What's going on?

251
00:20:30,340 --> 00:20:32,237
I can't get into that right now.

252
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:33,580
Now, listen, Kirito.

253
00:20:33,740 --> 00:20:36,093
I need you to locate a girl named Alice.

254
00:20:36,380 --> 00:20:38,597
Find her and take her to - I
don't have to look for her.

255
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:39,617
She's right here.

256
00:20:39,700 --> 00:20:40,530
You have her?

257
00:20:40,613 --> 00:20:41,715
You gotta be kidding.

258
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:43,317
That kid's awesome.

259
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:44,230
Yeah.

260
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:47,937
All right, once we're off the line,
I'll crank the FLA to a thousand.

261
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:50,917
Then take Alice and head
to the world's end altar.

262
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,460
I never heard of that place. That's okay.

263
00:20:53,760 --> 00:20:56,737
Just go out the eastern gate
and the altars due south.

264
00:20:56,820 --> 00:20:57,650
Sir!

265
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:02,237
Two of them are heading down the corridor.

266
00:21:02,320 --> 00:21:03,560
Port electric! What?

267
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:08,100
Be careful.

268
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:10,028
We just need the mains off.

269
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:13,717
Whatever you do, don't damage the
lines for the light cube cluster.

270
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:15,060
Would you relax, bro?

271
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:16,460
I know what to cut.

272
00:21:16,740 --> 00:21:17,600
We're screwed!

273
